From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sarol263@student.otago.ac.nz>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:22:04 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 40/51] Plutonium: downloads for the shells' tabs

EXO-TAB-FEATURES (docs/features/TAB_FEATURES.md, "Downloads"): the
profile's download manager already saves what tabs download, but its UI
(Ash notifications) doesn't show in shell mode, and files went to the
profile's own folder.

- PlutoniumDownloads (plutonium_downloads.{h,cc}) lists this session's
  downloads, each with the tab that started it and that tab's thread (its
  origin tag), kept after the tab closes. Tab::AttachHelpers() and the
  broker observe the profile's download manager.
- Where files go: ~/Downloads (the XDG download folder) in shell mode,
  unless a shell set a folder for the thread or a default for its own
  threads (SetDownloadFolder): "thread" (~/Downloads/<thread label>/) or a
  path. DownloadTargetDeterminer asks FolderFor() for downloads that don't
  prompt.
- Shells: "downloadadded", "downloadchanged", "downloadremoved"
  (BrowserDownloadEvent, the current ones replayed on subscribing),
  downloadCommand(id, pause|resume|cancel|open|show|keep|discard|remove)
  and setDownloadFolder(tag, folder).
- Open and show go to the helper (POST /v1/downloads/open), which opens
  the file or its folder in the download's thread.
- Agents: Plutonium.getDownloads, downloadCommand (not "keep": a dangerous
  file is the user's to keep), downloadAdded/Changed/Removed.
- A tab whose first navigation became a download closes, as Chrome closes
  such a tab in its tab strip (not an agent's tab).
