+// EXO-TAB-FEATURES (docs/features/TAB_FEATURES.md, "Downloads"): the shells'
+// downloads. Chrome's download manager already saves what tabs download; its
+// UI (Ash notifications on ChromeOS) doesn't show in shell mode. This lists
+// the downloads for the shells (navigator.windowBroker's "downloadadded",
+// "downloadchanged" and "downloadremoved") and agents (the DevTools Plutonium
+// domain), with the thread each came from: the origin tag of the tab that
+// started it, kept even after the tab closes.
+//
+// Where files go (FolderFor()): ~/Downloads (the XDG download folder), unless
+// a shell set a folder for the thread, or a default for its own threads
+// (SetFolder()): "thread" (~/Downloads/<thread label>/) or a path, such as a
+// ".downloads" folder in the thread's working directory. An agent's tab
+// downloads where the user's tabs in its thread do.
+//
+// A tab whose first navigation became a download (a link opened in a new tab)
+// closes, as Chrome closes such a tab in its tab strip. Downloads from earlier
+// runs (Chrome's history) aren't listed.
+class PlutoniumDownloads : public content::DownloadManager::Observer,
+                           public download::DownloadItem::Observer {
+ public:
+  // Downloads as JSON objects (ToValue()): {id, tabId, thread, url,
+  // filename, path, mime, receivedBytes, totalBytes, state ("in-progress",
